# {{project_title}}

> Generated with `aistrap` using the `mcp-server` template.

A standard Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that exposes tools and resources to AI assistants like Claude Desktop, Cursor, and AI agents over standard I/O (JSON-RPC 2.0).

## Project structure

```
{{project_name}}/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── config.py    # Environment settings
│   ├── main.py      # Stdio JSON-RPC event loop
│   ├── protocol.py  # JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol definitions
│   └── server.py    # MCP tools and resources dispatcher
├── config/
├── tests/
│   └── test_app.py
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
├── pytest.ini
├── README.md
└── requirements.txt
```

## Getting started

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env
```

## Run the server

```bash
python -m app.main
```

## Run tests

```bash
pytest
```

## Connecting to Claude Desktop or Cursor

Add this to your `claude_desktop_config.json`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{project_name}}": {
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["-m", "app.main"],
      "cwd": "/path/to/{{project_name}}"
    }
  }
}
```
